{
  "info": {
    "name": "User Management System API",
    "description": "REST endpoints for the User Management System. Start the app first (default http://localhost:8080).\n\nRun the folders IN ORDER (Collection Runner or one by one). Folder 1 saves the role ids into collection variables, and the other folders use them.\n\n1. Roles - read: lists roles and saves their ids.\n2. Users - read: list, search, get one, errors.\n3. Users - create, update, delete: uses its own test users and deletes them at the end. Checks status, createdAt and updatedAt.\n4. Roles - status rules: error cases and GUEST protection. Changes no data.\n5. Role deactivation flow: WARNING, this changes real data (see the folder description).\n\nEvery request has tests (see the Test Results tab).\n\nPasswords: creating a user needs a password (6+ characters with an uppercase letter, a lowercase letter, a number and a special character). When editing, leave it out to keep the current one. The API never sends a password back, only \"hasPassword\": true/false.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "runId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminRoleId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "managerRoleId", "value": "2" },
    { "key": "userRoleId", "value": "3" },
    { "key": "guestRoleId", "value": "4" },
    { "key": "guestUpdatedAt", "value": "" },
    { "key": "existingUserId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "testUserId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "testUser2Id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "testUserCreatedAt", "value": "" },
    { "key": "testUserUpdatedAt", "value": "" },
    { "key": "flowUserId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Roles - read",
      "description": "Reads the roles. The first request saves every role id into collection variables (adminRoleId, managerRoleId, userRoleId, guestRoleId), so run it before the other folders.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List roles - saves role ids (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const roles = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Has ADMIN, MANAGER, USER and GUEST', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(roles.map(r => r.name)).to.include.members(['ADMIN', 'MANAGER', 'USER', 'GUEST']);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Every role has status, updatedAt and userCount', () => {",
                  "    roles.forEach(r => {",
                  "        pm.expect(r.status).to.be.oneOf(['ACTIVE', 'INACTIVE']);",
                  "        pm.expect(r.updatedAt).to.be.a('string');",
                  "        pm.expect(r.userCount).to.be.a('number');",
                  "    });",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('GUEST is ACTIVE', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(roles.find(r => r.name === 'GUEST').status).to.eql('ACTIVE');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Save ids for the other folders, e.g. MANAGER -> managerRoleId",
                  "roles.forEach(r => pm.collectionVariables.set(r.name.toLowerCase() + 'RoleId', r.id));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('guestUpdatedAt', roles.find(r => r.name === 'GUEST').updatedAt);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/roles"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Users - read",
      "description": "Reads users. Changes no data.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List all users (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const users = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Returns a list', () => pm.expect(users).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('Every user has status, createdAt and updatedAt', () => {",
                  "    users.forEach(u => {",
                  "        pm.expect(u.status).to.be.oneOf(['ACTIVE', 'INACTIVE']);",
                  "        pm.expect(u.createdAt).to.be.a('string');",
                  "        pm.expect(u.updatedAt).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    });",
                  "});",
                  "// Compare to the millisecond: created_at keeps 7 decimals, updated_at keeps 6 (rounded)",
                  "const ms = t => t.substring(0, 23);",
                  "pm.test('updatedAt is never before createdAt', () => {",
                  "    users.forEach(u => pm.expect(ms(u.updatedAt) >= ms(u.createdAt), 'user ' + u.id).to.be.true);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('No user exposes a password, only hasPassword', () => {",
                  "    users.forEach(u => {",
                  "        pm.expect(u).to.not.have.any.keys('password', 'passwordHash');",
                  "        pm.expect(u.hasPassword).to.be.a('boolean');",
                  "    });",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Remember one real user for 'Get user by id'",
                  "if (users.length > 0) pm.collectionVariables.set('existingUserId', users[0].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Search users by name or email (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Every result has \"an\" in the name or email', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.json().forEach(u => {",
                  "        const text = (u.name + ' ' + u.email).toLowerCase();",
                  "        pm.expect(text).to.include('an');",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users?search=an"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get user by id (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const u = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Returns the requested user', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(u.id).to.eql(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('existingUserId')));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Has role, status, createdAt and updatedAt', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(u).to.include.keys('roleId', 'roleName', 'status', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{existingUserId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get user - not found (404)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('Message says not found', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.include('not found');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/999999"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get user - invalid id (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Message names the bad value', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.include('abc');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/abc"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Users - create, update, delete",
      "description": "Creates two test users (emails pm.test.<time>@example.com), tests status / createdAt / updatedAt and the error cases, then deletes the test users. Run the whole folder in order.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create user with status (201)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A new number each run, so the test emails are always unique",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('runId', Date.now());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Location header points to the new user', () => pm.response.to.have.header('Location'));",
                  "const u = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is ACTIVE and role is USER', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(u.status).to.eql('ACTIVE');",
                  "    pm.expect(u.roleName).to.eql('USER');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('createdAt and updatedAt are the same for a new user', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(u.updatedAt).to.eql(u.createdAt);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Password is saved but never sent back', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(u.hasPassword).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(u).to.not.have.any.keys('password', 'passwordHash');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('testUserId', u.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('testUserCreatedAt', u.createdAt);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('testUserUpdatedAt', u.updatedAt);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Test\",\n  \"email\": \"pm.test.{{runId}}@example.com\",\n  \"roleId\": {{userRoleId}},\n  \"status\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"password\": \"Test@123\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create user without status - defaults to ACTIVE (201)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const u = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('No status sent -> ACTIVE', () => pm.expect(u.status).to.eql('ACTIVE'));",
                  "pm.test('GUEST can be assigned', () => pm.expect(u.roleName).to.eql('GUEST'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('testUser2Id', u.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Test Two\",\n  \"email\": \"pm.test2.{{runId}}@example.com\",\n  \"roleId\": {{guestRoleId}},\n  \"password\": \"Test@123\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          }
        },
